 "_method": "Wikimedia Commons photos (640px thumbs) from '<taxon> in autumn/October/November' and '<taxon> in summer/July/August' categories (+ country/solitary/by-month subcats for sparse taxa), date-filtered by EXIF/metadata month (autumn: Oct-Nov; summer: Jun-Aug), Central European sources preferred, every photo visually checked (canopy of that taxon, no close-ups/bark/fruit/cultivars like copper beech, 'Frisia', 'Tristis'). Per image (top 75% of frame): drop sky (HSV hue 170-300 or V>0.85&S<0.35), V<0.15, S<0.2; 'green' = CIELAB hue angle 103-220 deg (HSV 70-160 was tested and misclassifies dark olive canopy, which sits at HSV 50-75). Per-image median in CIELAB, then per-taxon median across images. autumn_hex = median of non-green leaf pixels (all leaf pixels for Fraxinus and Alnus, which drop leaves green); summer_hex = median of green pixels. *_lit_hex = same but only the brighter half (by L*) of the masked pixels in each photo, i.e. sunlit leaves rather than crown self-shadow. green_fraction_autumn = green/(all leaf) pixels in the top half of frame, median over images; biased low because photos were chosen to show autumn colour, and includes some background vegetation.",
 "_class_8b_note": "Fagus sylvatica measured separately as class '8b' (alongside Carpinus = 8).",
